Cramapple Content & Teaching Methodology

This blueprint governs the structural conversion of unorganized academic content into deterministic, high-scoring exam text outputs without relying on generic summary text blocks.

---

## 1. The D→E→P Metacognitive Framework

Advanced Placement natural science scoring rubrics reward structural cause-and-effect tracking over simple conceptual recall. The product maps all curriculum units directly onto this structured execution layout.

| Step | Structural Target | Execution Directive |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **D**efine | Scientific Boundary Identification | The student must isolate the exact structural properties or core definitions relevant to the prompt (e.g., *Surface-area-to-volume ratio equations*). |
| **E**xplain | Causal Chain Step Tracking | The student must trace the sequential progression step-by-step. Causal logical shortcuts are flagged instantly by the parser. |
| **P**redict | System Disturbance Outcome | The student must project the precise biological outcome of a structural mutation or environmental shift. |

---

## 2. Logic-Gap Protocol & Bracket Marker Inversion

The application prevents students from taking causal shortcuts (e.g., writing *"The temperature rises, so the cell dies"* without explaining the structural breakdown).

[ Student Input String ] ──> "High heat causes the cell to instantly lose its function."
│
▼
[ Logic-Gap Evaluation Engine ]
Matches missing token steps between "High heat" and "lose function"
│
▼
[ Inverted UI Output Render ] ──> "High heat [...] denatures the active site shape,
breaking substrate affinity and causing the cell
to lose its function."


*   **Bracket Marker UI Feedback Layer:** When a gap is flagged, the application renders an inline bracket placeholder (`[...]`) directly within the student's text string, highlighting exactly where a logical step was skipped.
*   **Socratic Remediator Prompt Injection:** The system inserts an immediate sub-challenge below the text input:
```text
    Your chain has a logic gap at [...]. You stated the environmental stressor and the terminal outcome, but skipped the molecular interaction. What happens to the tertiary protein bonds when kinetic energy exceeds baseline limits?
    ```

